# subalpine_fir_floor_a: a clump of three subalpine firs far below, on a
# basin's floor (the rim scene's benches and tarn shores; BUILD_PLAN S5
# brief B9), drawn at floor scale for the wide pixel (11.2): three spires
# 5, 4 and 3 rows tall, each one column wide at the tip and stepping out a
# column at a time to its foot, so a far fir reads as a small tapering
# spire and the clump as three of them, never a block, a post or a comb.
# Each spire's shadow side spruce (11) on the left, its lit side forest
# (12) on the right, so the spires keep their shape at every hour (ink and
# spruce at dusk, blue hour and night). No trunks. The anchor, 0,0, is the
# tallest spire's foot. 11 wide, 5 tall.
# the tallest, in the middle
C 11  L 0,-4 0,0  L -1,-1 -1,0
C 12  L 1,-2 1,0  L 2,0
# the second, on the right
C 11  L 4,-3 4,0  L 3,0
C 12  L 5,-1 5,0
# the smallest, on the left
C 11  L -4,-2 -4,0  L -5,0
C 12  L -3,-1 -3,0
